  steps:
    1. Pick grid size in range. Pick N=2-7 rectangles.
    2. Pick winner rectangle dims (3-10 x 3-10), assign 1-3 markers (colors from {4,6}).
    3. For each non-winner rectangle, pick dims (3-10 x 3-10), assign marker_count > winner's count (ensure runner-up has >=winner+1 markers).
    4. Place all rectangles on the grid with >=1 bg gap between bboxes; use rejection or greedy packing. Fill=1 everywhere except marker positions.
    5. Scatter marker pixels randomly within each rectangle's area.
    6. Output = crop of the winner rectangle.
```
