<description>
Compute a grey result bar by adding teal bar heights and subtracting red bar heights.

Input structure
- The grid has a dominant background and several bottom-aligned one-cell-wide vertical bars.
- Teal bars are positive operands; red bars are negative operands.
- The penultimate column is an empty result slot.

Rule
- Keep every input bar unchanged.
- Compute result height = total teal bar height - total red bar height.
- Paint that many bottom cells of the penultimate column grey.

Key insight
- The bars encode arithmetic by height, with color providing the sign.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "bottom-aligned one-cell-wide teal and red vertical bars",
  "dst": "empty penultimate column result slot",
  "transform": "paint a bottom-aligned grey result bar whose height is total teal bar height minus total red bar height"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid:
    background: ORANGE (7)
    height: 6-12
    width: 2*N + 3, where N = number of operand bars
  bars:
    count: 2-6 operand bars (N)
    placement: bottom-aligned, 1-cell-wide vertical bars at odd columns 1, 3, ..., 2N-1
    even_columns: all even columns (0, 2, ..., W-1) are background
    colors: each bar is TEAL (8, positive) or RED (2, negative); at least 1 teal bar
    bar_height: 1 to H-1 per bar (row 0 always background above tallest bar [observed])
  result_slot:
    column: W-2 (penultimate); empty in input, last column W-1 also empty
    gap: 2 columns between last operand bar and result column
  output:
    unchanged: all input bars preserved
    result_bar: bottom-aligned grey (5) bar at column W-2
    result_height: sum(teal heights) - sum(red heights); must be in [1, H]
generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    - pick N (2-6) and H (6-12)
    - set W = 2*N + 3
    - for each of N bars, assign color (TEAL or RED) ensuring >=1 TEAL
    - pick result_height r in [1, H-1]
    - assign bar heights in [1, H-1] such that sum(teal) - sum(red) = r
    - construct grid: fill H x W with ORANGE, place each bar bottom-aligned at column 2*i+1
    - place grey result bar (height r) at column W-2 to get the output
    - remove the grey bar to get the input
  height_assignment: |
    pick sum(teal) = r + sum(red), then distribute among teal bars (each >= 1, <= H-1);
    pick sum(red) freely, distribute among red bars similarly;
    ensure no bar exceeds H-1 and result fits in [1, H]
```
